  "body": "Direct-PR: one-test fix that unblocks the first ledger batch (#674); follow-up to #621 (#620).\n\n**Problem.** `RealBodiesTest.test_real_bodies_fold_or_are_reported` (in `scripts/tests/test_docs_ledger.py`) copies the live `docs/CHANGELOG-LEGACY.md` and GAP file, then folds the merged bodies of #590, #604 and #607 into them. Ledger PR #674 already folds those PRs. On its head the rows exist, so #607's new `GAP-596` is refused and the \"Fixture tooling tests\" check fails: `[604] != [604, 607]`.\n\n**Change.** Before folding, the test removes the #604 and #607 changelog rows and the `GAP-596` row from its copies. The copies then match the state before the batch, whatever the checkout. #604's in-place edit is applied again and reported as \"already applied\".\n\n**Tests.** `python3 -m unittest discover -s scripts/tests` passes, with and without `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true`, both on dev-swift and with #674's two ledger files checked out. Before the change it failed on the second state.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CJ4JPCeiaUyzcb2HYv)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Updated a documentation ledger test to exclude selected changelog entries before checking how pull request descriptions are folded or reported.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
