   "body": "<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n<a href=\"https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/679?scope=ghh_OusAJGA4HG8ljoOV0wJvVx8NmnZIjc2DdjmxOu0xZWA&amp;cs_source=review_comment\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change.svg\"><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change.svg\" alt=\"Explain Change →\" height=\"32\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Walkthrough</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\nThe real-body ledger test now removes changelog rows for PRs 604 and 607 and the GAP-596 row from copied files before folding the real PR bodies.\n\n**Changes: Real-body ledger test**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|:---|:---|\n|**Filter real-body test inputs** <br> `scripts/tests/test_docs_ledger.py`|The test imports `re` and removes rows for PRs 604 and 607 and GAP-596 from copied files before folding the real PR bodies.|\n\n<!-- change_assessment_start -->\n**Estimated code review effort:** 2 (Simple) | ~8 minutes\n\n<!-- change_assessment_commit:\"5e3ae9459755983813e8843a98758eb6745a1f7d\" -->\n<!-- change_assessment_priority:{\"version\":1,\"urgency\":\"p3\",\"manual\":false} -->\n**Change:** Other\n<!-- change_assessment_end -->\n\n**Possibly related PRs**\n- [ezzz/HFRnow#621](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/621): This PR modifies a real-body test and ledger folding behavior introduced in PR `#621`.\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Merge Risk:</strong> <strong><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/risk-unassessed-16.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> Minimal</strong> · up to <code>5e3ae</code></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\n<!-- final_review_risk_start -->\n<!-- final_review_risk_label\n**Merge Risk:** **⚪ Minimal** · up to `5e3ae`\n-->\n<!-- final_review_risk_coverage:{\"sourceCommitId\":\"5e3ae9459755983813e8843a98758eb6745a1f7d\",\"coveredCommitId\":\"5e3ae9459755983813e8843a98758eb6745a1f7d\",\"kind\":\"reviewed\"} -->\n\nThe change adjusts test inputs without changing the live ledgers. No merge-blocking regression was established.\n<!-- final_review_risk_end -->\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Pre-merge checks: <sup><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-counter-passed-14-v2.svg\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" align=\"middle\" alt=\"Passed\" title=\"Passed\"></picture></sup> 4 · <sup><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-counter-failed-14-v2.svg\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" align=\"middle\" alt=\"Failed\" title=\"Failed\"></picture></sup> 1</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\n<strong><sup><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-counter-failed-14-v2.svg\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" align=\"middle\" alt=\"Failed\" title=\"Failed\"></picture></sup> Failed checks: 1 warning</strong>\n\n|     Check name     |                                              Status                                              | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                               | Resolution                                                                         |\n| :---------------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------: | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Docstring Coverage | ![Warning](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-warning.svg) | Docstring coverage is 0.00% which is insufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%. Docstring coverage is scoped to functions touched by this diff with cyclomatic complexity of at least 2. Documentat… | Write docstrings for the functions missing them to satisfy the coverage threshold. |\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong><sup><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-counter-passed-14-v2.svg\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" align=\"middle\" alt=\"Passed\" title=\"Passed\"></picture></sup> Passed checks: 4 passed</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\n|         Check name         |                                             Status                                             | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| :------------------------ | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------: | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|      Description Check     | ![Passed](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-passed.svg) | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                                                               |\n|         Title check        | ![Passed](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-passed.svg) | The title \"Ledger test: fold the real bodies into the pre-batch state\" matches the main change. The PR edits the test RealBodiesTest.test_real_bodies_fold_or_are_reported in scripts/tests/test_docs_le… |\n|     Linked Issues check    | ![Passed](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-passed.svg) | Check skipped because no linked issues were found for this pull request.                                                                                                                                  |\n| Out of Scope Changes check | ![Passed](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-passed.svg) | Check skipped because no linked issues were found for this pull request.                                                                                                                                  |\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Full details: Title check</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\n**Explanation**\n\nThe title \"Ledger test: fold the real bodies into the pre-batch state\" matches the main change. The PR edits the test RealBodiesTest.test_real_bodies_fold_or_are_reported in scripts/tests/test_docs_ledger.py so that it removes the `#604` and `#607` changelog rows and the GAP-596 row from the copied files before folding the real PR bodies. That makes the copies represent the pre-batch state. The title is specific and accurate, and it is a single sentence. It names the test area and the purpose of the change. It is slightly dense in wording, but a teammate scanning history would understand the primary change.\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Full details: Docstring Coverage</strong></summary>\n<dl>